  "headline": "Early results released for municipal council races in Windsor, Ontario",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Early results from the municipal election in Windsor, Ontario, show various candidates leading in several council races. According to reporting from CBC Canada, the following results have been recorded for specific wards: Frazier Fathers leads Ward 2 with 80.91 per cent of the vote, Renaldo Agostino leads Ward 3 with 60.78 per cent, Angelo Marignani leads Ward 7 with 68.87 per cent, Gary Kaschak leads Ward 8 with 54.8 per cent, and Kieran McKenzie leads Ward 9 with 70.32 per cent. In Ward 10, Jim Morrison is in third place with 25.58 per cent of the vote. Additionally, Adam Ibrahim leads with 444 votes or 31.91 per cent, while Mark Masanovich is in second with 440 votes or 34.59 per cent."
    }
